  "response_text": "Include .c files is a bad idea as this can cause multiple definitions of the same function. This can happen if both .c files contain a .c file with the same definition. This would cause the compiler to crash as it would get confused. Another reason is that .h files are much shorter than .c files. If the .c file was included then it would have to copy over that entire .c file with the full definition to the next .c file. Whereas the header file contains just the format of the functions contained so it can compile much faster than compiling the .c file every time.\\n",
